FILE: minify.sh   (new file)

OLD_SECTION
(file did not exist)

NEW_SECTION
Bash script at the repository root. It reads the version from the core's
filename (src/vUX-core-<version>.js), clears dist/<version>/, runs a pinned
esbuild (0.28.2, fetched through npx) over vUX-*.js and src/*.js with
--minify --format=esm --target=es2017 --outbase=. --legal-comments=none,
copies assets/ and LICENSE alongside, and prints the before/after JS size.

REASON
The library had no way to ship a minified copy. Each file is minified on its own
rather than bundled because components load each other through relative dynamic
imports (vUX-formComponents.js -> ./vUX-toolTip.js, vUX-progressIndicator.js ->
./vUX-cShapes.js), so the output keeps the same names and layout as the source.
Export names and free globals are never renamed by the minifier, so the core's
promotion of helpers onto window still works. assets/ is copied because the core
resolves CSS through data-library-root + "/assets/". esbuild is pinned so two
runs of the script produce the same output.
